  "extractionNotes": "Quarter-time employee whose pay equals 1/4 of the minimum wage (752.50 / 872.50 / 900.00, later 1060.50). Employer sick pay 2023-09-21..2023-10-23, then ZUS sickness benefit 2023-10-24..2023-12-14 and 2023-12-18..2024-04-08 (ZUS note: all benefits granted and paid). Birth 2024-04-09; maternity follows sickness without a gap, so the base carries over from the sickness window 2022-09..2023-08 (September 2022 incomplete: hire on 2022-09-12 per the title register; a second Z-3 says 2022-09-21). ZUS notice of 2024-07-15 confirms maternity benefit 2024-04-09..2025-04-07 and, citing the top-up rule, raises it to the 1000 zl parental-benefit level from 2024-04-09 because the April net amount was lower and no other title exists; it requires a single-title statement, which is in the file. Leave application date on the Z-3 is 2024-04-30 (day 21). The ZAM (full-length declaration ticked) splits maternity to 2024-08-26 and parental from 2024-08-27, and declares the father's parental leave 2024-05-13..2024-06-14, described in a separate statement as part of his own 9 weeks, taken concurrently. Amounts not printed; whether the part-time minimum-wage floor applies is left to the engine."
